Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.65,0:05:29.91,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnTimes New Roman\b1\1a&HFF&\shad0\3c&HCFCFCF&\pos(218,15)}Judo
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.97,0:05:29.91,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(325,0)\pos(406,148)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H070207&\3c&HFFFFFF&\shad0}Yamada Albert
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.91,0:05:31.91,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\c&HF9ECD9&\3c&H573C2C&\shad0\fs16\b1\frx48\fry4\frz151.6\pos(104,300)}Select who will participate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.91,0:05:31.91,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\c&HFFFFFF&\shad0\bord0\fs20\b1\frx48\fry4\frz151.6\pos(412.364,329.455)}Selecting
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.91,0:05:35.64,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnTimes New Roman\b1\1a&HFF&\shad0\3c&HFFFFFF&\pos(268,73.667)\frx12\fry14\fs16\frz349.7\bord1.5}Judo
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.68,0:05:36.91,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs30\c&H7344E5&\bord0\shad0\pos(362.182,81.455)\frx16\fry22\frz349.3}Forfeit
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.21,0:05:57.85,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,It's unlikely to work, but shouldn't \Nyou complain to the school staff?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.61,0:06:01.85,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,I want to take this forward, as a lesson.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.51,0:06:03.57,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.41,0:06:08.81,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,If this had happened during a crucial \Nmoment in our second or third years,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.81,0:06:11.86,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,it could have been disastrous.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.86,0:06:14.64,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,But in this moment, we can handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.49,0:06:18.62,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.95,0:06:24.35,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Then there's no need for an outsider \Nlike me to poke my nose in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.35,0:06:27.88,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,I hear you guys put up a really good fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.18,0:06:30.72,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,You're really getting better and better.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.72,0:06:32.94,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,I guess we'd better watch our backs!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.94,0:06:35.01,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,On that subject...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.59,0:06:40.96,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,To be blunt, I'd like to dissolve \Nour alliance moving into next year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.09,0:06:46.27,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Yeah, I had a feeling you might say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.79,0:06:47.71,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.48,0:06:51.75,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,I wonder if we could preserve \Nit for now, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.13,0:06:56.57,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Maybe once the gap in our \Nclass points gets tighter—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.69,0:06:56.57,Main_Top,Horikita,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.64,0:07:03.79,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,My goal for next year is to \Nbecome Class B or higher.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.12,0:07:12.30,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,And in order to overtake Class A, \NI intend to go after points, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.19,0:07:16.05,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,You're serious about this, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.47,0:07:18.86,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'm grateful to you for
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.86,0:07:22.81,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,bringing the alliance proposal to us \Nback when we were hopeless.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.83,0:07:28.26,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,But next year we'll be genuine enemies, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.03,0:07:31.07,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Class B will be giving all we have, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.44,0:07:32.23,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.35,0:07:46.59,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Are you going to the graduation party?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.59,0:07:51.84,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,If you're asking whether I'm going \Nto see my brother, I don't plan to.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.84,0:07:54.82,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I thought you'd finally found \Nit in yourself to speak to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.08,0:07:57.10,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,How is any of that your business?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.40,0:08:01.85,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm going to go see him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.87,0:08:06.02,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Is that an issue for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.59,0:08:08.06,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.06,0:08:10.60,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,You're free to see my brother if you want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.00,0:08:17.44,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But first...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.03,0:08:20.51,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I suppose I'll do what I ought to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.30,0:08:26.98,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I'm on suspension for \Nallegations of impropriety.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.37,0:08:30.88,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I don't think I have the power to \Nstop Acting Chairman Tsukishiro.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.24,0:08:34.02,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If I act directly against his plans,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.02,0:08:39.12,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,it could end up spreading the \Nchaos through the entire school.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.01,0:08:43.91,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Are you saying you want a sponsor \Nwho can actively oppose him?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.72,0:08:48.35,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Mr. Mashima may be the ticket, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.65,0:08:52.44,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,The school is full of surveillance cameras.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.01,0:08:55.89,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Leave the setting for the discussion to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.93,0:08:58.63,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.11,0:08:59.88,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Well, then—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.88,0:09:02.88,Italics,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Can I ask you one final question?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.49,0:09:04.21,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.67,0:09:10.15,Main,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,You came to this school \Nhoping for a normal life.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.69,0:09:14.11,Main,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Have you thought about what \Nwill happen when you graduate?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.61,0:09:17.16,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,My destiny is set in stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.88,0:09:22.11,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,After I graduate, I'll go \Nback to where I came from,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.47,0:09:25.75,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,and act as a mentor there, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.18,0:09:31.94,Main,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,So you're also here despite an \Nacceptance of your eventual fate?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.94,0:09:37.19,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's all the more reason why I intend \Nto protect these three years I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.79,0:09:46.48,Main,Chairman Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I hope this school will be a positive \Nexperience you'll carry with you all your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.29,0:09:53.50,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,175)\frz0\c&H171B14&\3c&H5A4B40&\shad0\fnTimes New Roman\fs16\pos(488,240)}Reception Room
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.10,0:09:57.63,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm coming in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.14,0:10:10.35,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,A directive from Chairman \NSakayanagi and a secret meeting
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.35,0:10:12.65,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,just before the graduation party.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.23,0:10:15.40,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,Whatever this is, it must be rather important.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.75,0:10:18.53,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,This is a rather reckless thing you've done.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.84,0:10:21.92,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I thought you wanted to live a peaceful life?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.55,0:10:27.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I have something important to discuss \Nregarding Chairman Tsukishiro.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.09,0:10:29.41,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.80,0:10:35.42,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Chairman Sakayanagi's suspension and \Nthe results of the final special exam...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.42,0:10:40.74,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,What if I were to tell you Chairman \NTsukishiro set them all up himself?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.32,0:10:55.56,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,I'm not entirely convinced of your story,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.80,0:10:59.57,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,but if it's true, it's not \Nsomething we can let slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.08,0:11:04.42,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,But Mr. Mashima, just this \Nmorning he gave you a pay cut
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.42,0:11:07.30,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,for breaking the rules of \Nthe final special exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.30,0:11:09.58,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,A pay cut for breaking the rules?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.58,0:11:12.46,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,For the judo competition \Nbetween Class B and Class D,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.72,0:11:16.96,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,the student chosen by \NClass D was Yamada Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.20,0:11:18.59,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.59,0:11:23.22,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,That could have been a dangerous \Nmatch, had it gone through.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.53,0:11:27.81,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,So Mr. Mashima used his \Njudgment to dub it a forfeit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.16,0:11:31.56,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The acting chairman didn't \Nlike that, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.56,0:11:35.60,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,He doesn't like the teachers \Nusing their discretion, I guess?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.02,0:11:39.21,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,If I think a situation's dangerous \Nto the students, I'll stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.52,0:11:41.61,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,If their behavior is wrong, I'll correct it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.61,0:11:45.61,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,Teachers have to be able \Nto protect their students!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.40,0:11:48.62,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,It appears he can't be stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.28,0:11:54.73,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,If Mr. Mashima agrees to this, \Nthen I'll help you, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.97,0:11:57.99,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,It sounds like we have an agreement.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.44,0:12:03.38,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I intend to take your side for \Nnow as well, Ayanokoji-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.38,0:12:10.39,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Only until the acting \Nchairman is gone, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.93,0:12:17.06,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,If he ever gets in the way of Class A, \NI'll brutally slap him down.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.49,0:12:18.72,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.72,0:12:21.09,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The graduation party will begin soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.51,0:12:23.87,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,You students should leave first.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.34,0:12:27.07,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,We'll leave separately later.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.70,0:12:33.04,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Honestly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.04,0:12:36.04,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,He's brought a difficult \Nproblem to our doorstep.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.65,0:12:41.67,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,You really think taking out \NActing Chairman Tsukishiro will end it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.05,0:12:43.67,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.99,0:12:48.59,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,There's no guarantee they won't \Nsend another assassin after him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.59,0:12:52.98,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,If that were to happen, it could spread \Nbeyond Ayanokoji's individual problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.98,0:12:54.68,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,and affect the whole class year...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.11,0:12:59.69,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,maybe even the entire school.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.08,0:13:02.44,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,It's truly a quagmire.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.71,0:13:07.23,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,I guess we should just hope \Nmy worst fear won't come true.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.09,0:13:09.36,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I suppose.
